00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:26.250
episode

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:26.250
"Now,

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:26.250
The Tennis Court Oath"

00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:32.450
<i>On June 17,</i>

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:36.520
<i>with several representatives from the First and Second Estate joining their ranks,</i>

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:40.180
<i>the Third Estate representatives passed a resolution, declaring themselves the National Assembly.</i>

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:45.140
Hurrah to the National Assembly!

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:54.510
National Assembly?

00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:56.470
What exactly is this National Assembly?

00:04:56.980 --> 00:05:00.450
Claiming to be the true representatives of
France, the commoners' representatives...

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:02.450
...concocted this assembly on their own,

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:05.720
by brushing aside the First and Second Estate
representatives of the Estates-General!

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:09.190
But I've heard several representatives
of the nobility and clergy...

00:05:09.190 --> 00:05:11.560
...have joined this National Assembly?

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:14.200
They're no longer members of
the nobility or the clergy.

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:16.700
They're nothing but vile mongrels
that grovel down to the commoners.

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:19.530
Your Majesty, if you allow the Estates-General
to continue on like this,

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:22.090
the commoners' representatives
will get even more arrogant!

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:31.680
Close the entrances to the Estates-General?

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:34.880
Yes, close all the entrances immediately.

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:37.520
This is an order from His Majesty, the King.

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:40.860
But if we do that, the representatives
won't be able to get inside.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:41.620
Indeed.

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:44.460
The Estates-General will be forced to adjourn.

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:45.630
That doesn't make sense.

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:47.530
The decision to convene and
dissolve the Estates-General,

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:50.670
can only be made by the Estates-General,
and the Estates-General alone.

00:05:50.670 --> 00:05:52.330
Even if it's His Majesty's orders...

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:55.300
That's why I'm ordering you to seal it off!

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:57.960
His Majesty never mentioned anything
about it being dissolved!

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:02.210
I've given you an order, Brigadier Jarjayes.

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:04.150
Make sure everything is closed securely.

00:06:04.150 --> 00:06:06.010
Even a kitten mustn't sneak in.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:08.600
With all due respect, General Bouillé,

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:12.750
the assembly members are representatives, who have
been rightfully elected by the people of France.

00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:16.650
Doing such a thing would be nothing
but an insult to them!

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:18.760
The people exist for His Majesty!

00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:20.330
The representatives exist for His Majesty!

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:22.230
And so do we, nobles!

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:24.110
Or am I mistaken, Brigadier Jarjayes?

00:06:25.670 --> 00:06:26.320
However, Your Excellency—!

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:27.990
That's enough, Oscar!

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:31.570
I didn't summon you here to have a debate!

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:33.310
I did so to give you an order!

00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:36.810
Listen, it's neither you or I
that's closing the assembly hall.

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:38.000
It's His Majesty's will!

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.750
All right, you may go now.

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:41.580
I'll hear your report later.

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:42.350
Yes!

00:06:45.890 --> 00:06:47.520
Brigadier Jarjayes!

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:49.460
Is your father well?

00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:50.950
I haven't seen him in a while.

00:06:51.630 --> 00:06:52.790
I see.

00:06:52.790 --> 00:06:54.060
Please excuse me.

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:01.200
What to do... André? Alain?

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:03.440
There's nothing to think about, Commander.

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:04.670
We were given an order.

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:05.940
We don't have a choice in the matter.

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:10.220
But the more dirty tricks they use,

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:12.660
the more impassioned we,
the commoners, will get.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:25.930
Hey, they're blocking the representatives
from going inside.

00:07:25.930 --> 00:07:27.660
How will they have an assembly then?!

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:30.260
This must be the royals and
nobles doing! Damn them!

00:07:31.770 --> 00:07:34.260
Let me speak to the person in charge.

00:07:39.510 --> 00:07:40.580
Hear me out!

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:42.980
The representatives here
have all borrowed money,

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:46.680
renting carriages and eating frugally so
that they could travel the distance!

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:48.160
There isn't any time to waste!

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:51.020
Open the chamber doors and
let us go inside at once!

00:07:51.020 --> 00:07:53.820
We still have a mountain
of issues we must discuss!

00:07:56.820 --> 00:07:59.260
Robespierre, it's pointless to
try and reason with them!

00:07:59.260 --> 00:08:02.230
They're nothing but puppets
that only move on command!

00:08:02.860 --> 00:08:06.130
If we can't gather here,
let's gather at Jeu de Paume instead!

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:07.000
Jeu de Paume...

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:08.590
Right! That's a large enough space!

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:11.010
I see! Jeu de Paume!

00:08:11.010 --> 00:08:12.010
What a brilliant idea!

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:13.740
All right, Gentlemen!

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:15.140
Let's go to Jeu de Paume!

00:08:17.110 --> 00:08:18.720
Jeu de Paume!

00:08:19.080 --> 00:08:20.510
Jeu de Paume!

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:23.310
Jeu de Paume!

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:27.020
<i>Jeu de Paume.</i>

00:08:27.020 --> 00:08:30.930
<i>They were referring to where Jeu de Paume,
a precursor of tennis, was played.</i>

00:08:30.930 --> 00:08:35.330
<i>Due to its immense popularity at the time,
courts were being built all across France.</i>

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:38.970
We have been driven out of the assembly hall!

00:08:38.970 --> 00:08:41.830
This is the true intent of the King
and the nobles who surround him!

00:08:42.190 --> 00:08:44.340
However, no matter what force they may use,

00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:46.300
they cannot crush our National Assembly!

00:08:46.910 --> 00:08:47.910
Gentlemen!

00:08:47.910 --> 00:08:52.010
Let us pledge our hearts, hands
and voices together as one!

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:54.760
Our National Assembly, run by
the people, for the people,

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:59.230
will not be dissolved until the day a constitution
for the people has been enacted!

00:09:05.830 --> 00:09:09.110
<i>June 20, 1789.</i>

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:15.570
<i>This was the famous ''Tennis Court Oath,'' which
signaled the beginning of the French Revolution.</i>

00:09:19.340 --> 00:09:20.790
Was I right or what, Commander?

00:09:21.180 --> 00:09:25.750
The more the oppressed are forced to suffer,
the more impassioned they become.

00:09:26.550 --> 00:09:29.470
You nobles can never seem to understand that.

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:40.260
I am Army Colonel Choiseul la Baume.

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:46.150
By the order of General Bouillé, I'll be directing
the entry of the representatives today.

00:09:46.430 --> 00:09:50.000
<i>In an effort to restore order to
the chaotic situation in one move,</i>

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:54.570
<i>the King summoned the representatives of
the Three Estates to gather once again.</i>

00:09:55.380 --> 00:10:01.680
<i>Furthermore, of the closed assembly hall,
only one front entrance door had been reopened.</i>

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:05.520
<i>The representatives were only allowed to
enter the assembly hall one by one.</i>

00:10:09.820 --> 00:10:12.060
Next, Bishop Fouchet.

00:10:12.060 --> 00:10:12.840
Please enter.

00:10:15.130 --> 00:10:16.840
Duke Châtelet, please enter.

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:19.130
Count Duplas.

00:10:19.130 --> 00:10:20.800
Bishop Le Faivre.

00:10:21.370 --> 00:10:22.940
Count Delage.

00:10:22.940 --> 00:10:24.370
Baron Meunier.

00:10:24.370 --> 00:10:25.470
Duke Clair.

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:27.810
Viscount Rosières... Ah, please wait.

00:10:27.810 --> 00:10:28.480
You are...?

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:30.770
Third Estate representative, Capelle-Brunelle.

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:33.340
My apologies. Please wait until I call your name.

00:10:35.850 --> 00:10:38.120
Next, Duke d'Antoide, please enter.

00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:39.490
Please state your name.

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:41.790
Third Estate representative, Guillaume Nogaret.

00:10:41.790 --> 00:10:43.530
My apologies. Please wait little while longer.

00:10:46.190 --> 00:10:50.540
<i>Soon, everyone began to realize
the strangeness of the situation.</i>

00:10:53.870 --> 00:10:56.510
H-Hey, why aren't they letting the
Third Estate representatives go in?

00:10:56.510 --> 00:10:58.310
Why are they making them wait?

00:10:58.310 --> 00:11:00.040
They'll get soaked at this rate!

00:11:00.710 --> 00:11:01.640
Hey, you!

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:03.720
Hurry up and let our representatives in!

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:05.580
Next, Bishop Maillet!

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:07.210
Colonel Choiseul la Baume!

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:11.150
Why? Why aren't you calling
the Third Estate representatives?!

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:12.650
It's an order.

00:11:12.650 --> 00:11:15.620
I've been instructed to only allow the clergy
and nobility to enter through the front,

00:11:15.620 --> 00:11:17.980
and the commoners' representatives through the back.

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:18.530
What?!

00:11:19.130 --> 00:11:20.060
Duke Vilaine.

00:11:20.060 --> 00:11:21.500
Colonel la Baume!

00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:23.100
Can you not see them?

00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:26.660
Can you not see all these people who are patiently
waiting, while getting soaked in the rain?

00:11:27.490 --> 00:11:31.740
I'm just following orders, Brigadier Jarjayes.

00:11:31.740 --> 00:11:35.460
Just as you followed your orders and
sealed off the entrances the other day.

00:11:37.610 --> 00:11:39.410
Wh-What are you doing?!

00:11:39.410 --> 00:11:40.720
Stop.

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:43.180
Stop it, Brigadier Jarjayes.

00:11:44.250 --> 00:11:48.470
We aren't bothered by the wetness
or the cold from the rain.

00:11:49.960 --> 00:11:53.930
Plus, no matter how hard the rain comes
down our passion will not be extinguished.

00:11:53.930 --> 00:11:56.400
We are here because the people have elected us.

00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:58.950
Regardless of their insults and ill treatment
of us, our pride is unwavering!

00:12:00.440 --> 00:12:03.400
Though let me make one thing clear.

00:12:03.400 --> 00:12:05.440
We are neither dogs nor beggars.

00:12:05.440 --> 00:12:07.910
That's why we'll never use
the back door as our entrance!

00:12:10.650 --> 00:12:12.450
Did you hear that, Brigadier Jarjayes?

00:12:12.450 --> 00:12:14.380
They choose to stand in the rain!

00:12:14.380 --> 00:12:16.290
It's not my responsibility!

00:12:20.620 --> 00:12:21.920
French Guardsmen!

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:26.480
Open every front entrance door and guide the representatives into the assembly hall immediately!

00:12:27.500 --> 00:12:28.590
You got it!

00:12:29.400 --> 00:12:30.130
Yeah!

00:12:40.410 --> 00:12:41.680
Brigadier Jarjayes!

00:12:41.680 --> 00:12:44.680
Do you mean to defy General Bouillé's order?!

00:12:44.680 --> 00:12:47.240
Not at all, Colonel la Baume.

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:49.830
Calm down and observe the crowd.

00:12:50.150 --> 00:12:53.250
If we make them wait any longer,
a riot will break out for certain.

00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:58.630
As the head of security, I did what I needed to
do to avoid having a disaster on our hands.

00:12:58.630 --> 00:13:01.720
Got that?! Now go back and
report this to General Bouillé!

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:26.750
Commander, all the representatives
are inside the assembly hall now.

00:13:27.290 --> 00:13:28.120
Well done.

00:13:28.560 --> 00:13:31.160
All right, everyone get back to your post.

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:32.220
Yes!

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:32.220
Yes!

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:35.060
Are we agreed, Your Majesty?

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:39.730
The monarchy is under threat.

00:13:39.730 --> 00:13:44.040
Already, two hundred representatives of
the nobility have joined the commoners,

00:13:44.040 --> 00:13:46.510
and are openly defying the royal household!

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:51.100
You must dissolve the National Assembly
with your effort and dignity!

00:13:59.210 --> 00:14:02.650
I... I have summoned the Estates-General,

00:14:03.200 --> 00:14:06.120
not something called the National Assembly!

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:10.070
Therefore, I order you to dissolve
the National Assembly at once!

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:14.270
Reconvene as the Estates-General and discuss
matters separately according to rank!

00:14:18.240 --> 00:14:20.380
Th-Therefore...

00:14:20.380 --> 00:14:22.210
There...fore...

00:14:23.220 --> 00:14:27.280
Therefore, I order you all to leave at once!

00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:39.690
What?!

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:41.060
Curse those traitors!

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:44.260
We cannot obey the King's order!

00:14:44.260 --> 00:14:45.070
That's right!

00:14:45.070 --> 00:14:48.170
We'll neither leave or be dissolved!

00:14:48.170 --> 00:14:49.240
That's right!

00:14:49.630 --> 00:14:51.300
They're sitting in!

00:14:51.300 --> 00:14:55.920
The representatives of the First and Second
Estate promptly left on His Majesty's order,

00:14:55.920 --> 00:14:58.820
but the National Assembly
faction are refusing to budge!

00:15:01.160 --> 00:15:02.990
Is Brigadier Jarjayes here?!

00:15:03.560 --> 00:15:07.020
Is the Commander of the French Guards
Company B, Brigadier Jarjayes here?!

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:09.820
I will now relay your order from General Bouillé!

00:15:09.820 --> 00:15:13.060
Bring your men and report to the command
center at Versailles at once!

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:22.790
Everyone, wait here.

00:15:23.390 --> 00:15:24.480
Commander, wait!

00:15:24.960 --> 00:15:29.440
We're supposed to be guarding the assembly hall,
so why did we get summoned here, too?

00:15:29.440 --> 00:15:31.490
I don't know either.

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:33.910
I somehow have a bad feeling about this.

00:15:39.210 --> 00:15:40.060
Hey, André.

00:15:40.720 --> 00:15:43.540
Go with her and see what this is about.

00:15:44.780 --> 00:15:45.480
All right.

00:15:50.520 --> 00:15:51.250
What is it?

00:15:52.060 --> 00:15:53.110
I'll go with you.

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:57.310
You stay out here!

00:15:57.310 --> 00:15:59.690
Come, Brigadier Jarjayes, please go inside.

00:16:04.230 --> 00:16:07.700
You and your subordinates in French Guards
Company B guarding the assembly hall,

00:16:07.700 --> 00:16:09.190
I'm relieving you of your duty.

00:16:10.270 --> 00:16:11.570
Please explain why!

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:12.340
Why?

00:16:12.340 --> 00:16:15.700
The decision to open the assembly hall entrances
against my orders, could be considered...

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:17.180
...as an act of insubordination!

00:16:17.180 --> 00:16:19.790
I could have you arrested and court-martialed.

00:16:20.150 --> 00:16:23.920
But I'm letting you off the hook this time by
just relieving you of your guarding duty.

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:26.500
I do not fear the military court!

00:16:27.360 --> 00:16:30.530
Your father is an old friend of mine.

00:16:30.530 --> 00:16:32.460
I'll pretend I didn't hear that.

00:16:35.930 --> 00:16:38.600
If there's nothing else to discuss,
I'll be leaving now.

00:16:38.600 --> 00:16:39.730
My men are waiting for me.

00:16:39.730 --> 00:16:41.570
No, I have a new mission for you.

00:16:41.570 --> 00:16:43.100
Now, listen closely.

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:46.730
The French Guards Company B are
to fully arm themselves at once,

00:16:46.730 --> 00:16:52.080
return to the assembly hall and remove every last
National Assembly faction member who's sitting-in!

00:16:52.650 --> 00:16:56.460
Remove them by any means, regardless
of their protests and reasons!

00:16:56.460 --> 00:17:00.420
I permit you to open fire and kill them, if need be!

00:17:01.930 --> 00:17:04.430
Open fire... and kill them, if need be...?!

00:17:04.430 --> 00:17:05.860
How could you ask this, Your Excellency?!

00:17:05.860 --> 00:17:07.960
The people elected them as
representatives of France!

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:09.930
Yet, you're ordering me to point a gun at them?!

00:17:09.930 --> 00:17:12.940
They're no representatives of the people!

00:17:12.940 --> 00:17:15.130
They're merely traitors defying His Majesty!

00:17:16.870 --> 00:17:21.560
Brigadier Jarjayes, arm your men and
head to the assembly hall at once!

00:17:21.980 --> 00:17:23.180
I refuse!

00:17:23.910 --> 00:17:25.380
Then, you leave me no choice.

00:17:25.380 --> 00:17:27.250
You are to be arrested for treason!

00:17:32.660 --> 00:17:35.860
I'll give my orders to your men myself.

00:17:35.860 --> 00:17:39.430
Do not let her step outside this room,
until I give further instructions, understand?!

00:17:39.430 --> 00:17:39.830
Yes!

00:18:03.050 --> 00:18:03.890
Don't move!

00:18:04.820 --> 00:18:06.190
Step away from the window.

00:18:06.190 --> 00:18:07.560
Face this way.

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:09.030
I won't resist arrest.

00:18:09.030 --> 00:18:11.700
There shouldn't be any harm in me looking
outside the window, Colonel la Baume.

00:18:11.700 --> 00:18:13.900
All right, raise your hands, then.

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:15.260
Fine.

00:18:17.430 --> 00:18:18.660
I want to see...

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:22.500
I want to see how my men will react
when they hear General Bouillé's orders.

00:18:33.380 --> 00:18:36.050
French Guards Company B, fall in!

00:18:42.460 --> 00:18:44.730
All right, I will now issue your orders!

00:18:44.730 --> 00:18:49.940
Company B will fully arm themselves and storm
the Estates-General assembly hall at once!

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:52.440
You are to do away with
every last unlawful squatter!

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:53.730
Wh-What?!

00:18:54.670 --> 00:18:59.730
Go back to your barracks, fully arm yourselves
and gather back here in 10 minutes!

00:19:01.010 --> 00:19:02.050
What are you waiting for?!

00:19:02.050 --> 00:19:02.980
Hurry up and go!

00:19:02.980 --> 00:19:03.700
Now, run!

00:19:06.980 --> 00:19:08.450
Wait, everyone!

00:19:11.150 --> 00:19:14.750
We promised Commander Oscar
we'd wait for her here!

00:19:15.360 --> 00:19:17.710
Don't you leave until our commander comes back!

00:19:18.660 --> 00:19:19.860
What are you all doing?!

00:19:19.860 --> 00:19:23.680
Are you defying the orders of
the Chief General of the Army?!

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:26.300
Who gives a damn, if he's the Chief General of the Army!

00:19:26.300 --> 00:19:28.500
We don't take orders from this guy!

00:19:29.240 --> 00:19:32.400
We only take orders from our commander!

00:19:34.950 --> 00:19:37.380
All right! I'm staying here with Squad Leader Alain!

00:19:38.520 --> 00:19:39.320
Me, too!

00:19:39.620 --> 00:19:40.650
I'm staying, too!

00:19:40.650 --> 00:19:41.580
Yeah, me too!

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:50.420
There you have it, Chief General.

00:19:51.700 --> 00:19:56.460
We, Alain de Soissons and eleven others, are
officially refusing to follow your order.

00:19:56.830 --> 00:19:58.070
Very well then!

00:19:58.070 --> 00:20:01.430
I'll show you what it means to
violate the order of the military!

00:20:26.630 --> 00:20:28.830
Your men are a mirror of their commander!

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:30.880
You have them trained well!

00:20:31.300 --> 00:20:33.830
Where are you taking my subordinates?

00:20:33.830 --> 00:20:35.210
To Abbaye Prison.

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:39.800
I'll request that all 12 men be executed
by firing squad in a military court!

00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:41.380
Executed by firing squad?!

00:20:41.380 --> 00:20:42.850
Brigadier Jarjayes!

00:20:42.850 --> 00:20:45.850
You should be worrying about your own
troubles instead of your subordinates!

00:20:46.550 --> 00:20:50.520
As for you, until His Majesty
hands down your punishment,

00:20:50.520 --> 00:20:54.420
your military rank will be forfeited and you'll
be detained in a special army prison!

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:56.830
Take her away!

00:20:56.830 --> 00:20:58.060
General Bouillé!

00:20:59.300 --> 00:21:01.200
Punishing me should be enough.

00:21:01.200 --> 00:21:03.740
Executing 12 subordinates by
firing squad is a grave mistake!

00:21:04.070 --> 00:21:07.470
No, those men will serve as an example.

00:21:07.470 --> 00:21:11.500
As further insubordination could threaten
the order of the entire French military.

00:21:12.540 --> 00:21:13.910
And one more thing!

00:21:13.910 --> 00:21:17.790
Storming the assembly hall with armed forces will
leave a deplorable stain in France's history!

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:22.550
In my mind, what's deplorable is the sit-in
by the National Assembly faction.

00:21:22.550 --> 00:21:23.800
You have nothing to worry.

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:26.510
The Royal Guards will remove the traitors.

00:21:27.490 --> 00:21:28.180
The Royal Guards?!

00:21:33.850 --> 00:21:35.300
Wh-What are you doing?!

00:21:35.300 --> 00:21:36.860
Forgive me, but you'll have to let me through.

00:21:46.610 --> 00:21:47.780
André!

00:21:49.380 --> 00:21:50.280
Oscar!

00:21:53.020 --> 00:21:53.810
André!

00:21:54.520 --> 00:21:55.120
Oscar!

00:22:17.410 --> 00:22:18.540
<i>Hurry André!</i>

00:22:18.540 --> 00:22:20.650
<i>The Royal Guards are going
to storm the assembly hall!</i>

00:22:20.980 --> 00:22:22.850
<i>We have to stop them at all costs!</i>

00:22:22.850 --> 00:22:24.010
<i>We have to!</i>

00:22:28.790 --> 00:22:33.580
To be continued

